## Context

First tranche of the conductor implementation (tracker 0550): discovery
only, no pipeline worker. Delivers R35's promise-half — knowing what
changed within a minute — before anything processes it. Also builds the
three fixtures every later tranche tests against, so they are shaped by
the first consumer rather than retrofitted.

## Relevant files

- SPEC.md §5.2.1 (ledger, keys), §5.2.4 (tick: item watermark, fulltext
  census diff, deletion subtraction, version-0 residue)
- Fork: `src/features/search/` at the reviewed SHA (UPSTREAM)

## Actions

1. Ledger schema: stage queues as rows (class, band, lane, timestamps),
   cursors, per-row claims with `claimed_input`, lease table. Priority is
   an ORDER BY over these columns — no scheduler object.
2. Reconcile tick: 60 s cadence, item `?since=` watermark scoped
   (oid, lib), full census diff for local fulltext, deletion subtraction
   every tick, back-off when Zotero is unreachable.
3. Fixtures: (a) record/replay fake of the Zotero local API — canned
   `?since=`, census, `/file` responses captured from the author's
   profile, plus programmable silence and latency; (b) synthetic library
   — ~50 items, controlled dateAdded, child notes and annotations, one
   monster attachment (~500 passages), one near-empty HTML snapshot;
   (c) injected clock — every "each N seconds" in the design reads it,
   no test sleeps.

## Test

- Red first: tick against the replay fixture discovers a new item, an
  edited fulltext version, and a deletion, each within one virtual tick.

## Verification

- [ ] Census diff flags the version-0 residue case per SPEC §5.2.4
- [ ] No wall-clock sleep anywhere in the test suite
- [ ] Positive control: each fixture demonstrated failing against a
      deliberately broken input before trusted (house discipline)

## Invariants

- Query path unchanged; upstream tests green on the fork branch.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Tick + ledger + fixtures merged on a fork branch, tests green
